incarceration rate.

00:29:17.122 --> 00:29:20.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, that's a
fairly damning indictment.

00:29:20.558 --> 00:29:25.563
Okay, where exactly
is it going wrong?

00:29:26.431 --> 00:29:29.167
Exactly, precisely procedurally

00:29:29.167 --> 00:29:30.668
so that we could fix it.

00:29:30.668 --> 00:29:33.037
Well, the whole thing has
to be burned to the ground.

00:29:33.037 --> 00:29:38.042
It's like, yeah, well, no
and you aren't thinking.

00:29:38.777 --> 00:29:40.011
So you're not helpful.

00:29:41.379 --> 00:29:43.047 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then you take a
problem like that apart,

00:29:43.047 --> 00:29:44.649
the differential
incarceration rate.

00:29:44.649 --> 00:29:46.284
Man, that's a rat's nest.

00:29:46.284 --> 00:29:47.986
It's complicated, man.

00:29:47.986 --> 00:29:50.021 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know it's tangled
up with slavery,

00:29:50.021 --> 00:29:51.823
it's tangled up with Jim Crow,

00:29:51.823 --> 00:29:54.225
it's tangled up with
differential exposure

00:29:54.225 --> 00:29:56.361
to literacy in childhood.

00:29:56.361 --> 00:29:59.664
It's tangled up with
single parent families,

00:29:59.664 --> 00:30:04.669
violent communities, the
drug war, drug policy,

00:30:06.204 --> 00:30:07.238
just to name a few.

00:30:07.238 --> 00:30:08.840
Then we could say

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:13.411
whatever implicit
racism still exists

00:30:13.411 --> 00:30:15.113
'cause that's not zero.

00:30:16.514 --> 00:30:19.651 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's very, very complicated
and people don't want

00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:23.855
a detailed on the ground
analysis of such problems.

00:30:23.855 --> 00:30:25.323
What they wanna do

00:30:25.323 --> 00:30:27.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
is label it with a low
resolution representation,

00:30:27.759 --> 00:30:30.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
so like a one pixel
representation,

00:30:30.528 --> 00:30:32.096 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then they
wanna contrast that

00:30:32.096 --> 00:30:34.732
with the wrong one
pixel representation.

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:36.568 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then they wanna feel
the moral virtue

00:30:36.568 --> 00:30:38.036
that they would have felt

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:39.704
if they had actually
solved the problem.

00:30:39.704 --> 00:30:41.673
- So how fix the resolution?

00:30:41.673 --> 00:30:44.576
And when I ask you this,
I include myself in this.

00:30:44.576 --> 00:30:46.811
I'm talking about news
every day on the show,

00:30:46.811 --> 00:30:49.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
I try to do it in the
most honest way possible.

00:30:49.547 --> 00:30:51.282
Obviously I have my biases,

00:30:51.282 --> 00:30:53.384 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm not pretending that
I have no opinions.

00:30:54.586 --> 00:30:57.388
But often when you get
bludgeoned over the head

00:30:57.388 --> 00:31:00.291 align:start size:88% position:13%
with sort of the low
resolution stuff enough,

00:31:00.291 --> 00:31:02.160 align:start size:84% position:16%
your resolution starts
getting screwed up.

00:31:02.160 --> 00:31:03.795 align:start size:88% position:13%
So how do we arbitrage-
- Yeah.

00:31:03.795 --> 00:31:05.029
- those two positions?

00:31:05.029 --> 00:31:05.930
- Well, it's not
just bias, right?

00:31:05.930 --> 00:31:07.498
It's not just bias.

00:31:07.498 --> 00:31:10.001 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's also heuristics and
there's a difference.

00:31:10.001 --> 00:31:13.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like a heuristic is a
functional simplification

00:31:13.438 --> 00:31:14.906 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we use heuristics
all the time.

00:31:14.906 --> 00:31:17.842
Like the image you see
of me as a heuristic

00:31:17.842 --> 00:31:19.177
'cause you are not seeing me.

00:31:19.177 --> 00:31:20.778 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, first of
all, I'm not there.

00:31:20.778 --> 00:31:23.548 align:start size:84% position:16%
Second of all, even
if you were seeing me,

00:31:23.548 --> 00:31:26.651
if we were in person, you'd
still be seeing a heuristic

00:31:26.651 --> 00:31:30.121
'cause you don't see
my subatomic structure.

00:31:30.121 --> 00:31:31.823
You don't see my
cellular structure.

00:31:31.823 --> 00:31:34.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't see the context
that I'm embedded in.

00:31:34.025 --> 00:31:37.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
You see an iconic image
that stands for the reality

00:31:37.362 --> 00:31:39.264
that's too complex to perceive.

00:31:39.264 --> 00:31:41.666
And so it's not easy to tell

00:31:41.666 --> 00:31:43.568
when you're using an
appropriate heuristic

00:31:43.568 --> 00:31:44.936
and the basic rule of thumb is

00:31:44.936 --> 00:31:48.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
use the simplest
thumbnail you can use

00:31:48.273 --> 00:31:50.475
that will get the job done.

00:31:50.475 --> 00:31:51.676
Now the question is...

00:31:51.676 --> 00:31:52.510
Then the question is,

00:31:52.510 --> 00:31:54.779
well, what is the job?

00:31:54.779 --> 00:31:56.381
And you have to ask yourself,

00:31:56.381 --> 00:31:58.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
well, how much honor
moral superiority

00:31:58.716 --> 00:32:00.618
are you actually striving for?

00:32:00.618 --> 00:32:03.187 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the answer
generally is, a lot.

00:32:03.187 --> 00:32:06.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's how a heuristic
turns into a bias

00:32:06.824 --> 00:32:09.127
and so it's partly ignorance.

00:32:09.127 --> 00:32:11.162
Some of it's malevolence
and willful blindness,

00:32:11.162 --> 00:32:12.397
but it's partly ignorance.

00:32:12.397 --> 00:32:14.899
It's like, you just
don't know, right?

00:32:14.899 --> 00:32:17.068
You don't even know
what you don't know.

00:32:17.068 --> 00:32:18.770
And then you think,

00:32:18.770 --> 00:32:20.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
well, isn't it interesting
that you have people

00:32:20.605 --> 00:32:24.575
who will pontificate about
fixing the electrical system,

00:32:24.575 --> 00:32:26.411
the power system,

00:32:26.411 --> 00:32:30.815
who couldn't wire up a plugin
in their house and you think,

00:32:30.815 --> 00:32:31.716
well, does that matter?

00:32:31.716 --> 00:32:33.151
It's like, well, yes.

00:32:33.151 --> 00:32:35.520 align:start size:97% position:3%
In some sense it does matter
because unless there's

00:32:35.520 --> 00:32:37.155
a chain of causality built

00:32:37.155 --> 00:32:39.424
from the highest
level abstractions

00:32:39.424 --> 00:32:41.659 align:start size:84% position:16%
right down to the
power outlet itself,

00:32:41.659 --> 00:32:45.396 align:start size:84% position:16%
the plan in some sense
is deeply flawed.

00:32:45.396 --> 00:32:47.598 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then we have
another problem, David.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:49.934
So look, when I worked
on this UN committee,

00:32:49.934 --> 00:32:52.070 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was on the Canadian
subsection of the committee.

00:32:52.070 --> 00:32:54.405
There was only one
Canadian subsection

00:32:54.405 --> 00:32:57.375
and I was pulled in by
the man who ran that,

00:32:57.375 --> 00:32:59.077
and I worked on it
for about two years

00:32:59.077 --> 00:33:00.244
and I was serious about it

00:33:00.244 --> 00:33:03.281 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I rewrote fair
chunks of that document,

00:33:03.281 --> 00:33:05.450
the sustainable goals guide,

00:33:05.450 --> 00:33:07.819
partly because it was
stuck in like 1985

00:33:07.819 --> 00:33:09.387 align:start size:81% position:19%
with this old cold
war mentality.

00:33:09.387 --> 00:33:10.321
It was terribly written.

00:33:10.321 --> 00:33:11.789
So I just rewrote a bunch of it.

00:33:11.789 --> 00:33:13.257
And what happened was,

00:33:13.257 --> 00:33:15.493 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
a lot of those rewrites
stuck and that was shocking.

00:33:15.493 --> 00:33:18.162 line:0%
It's like, what the hell?

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:19.397 line:0%
How did that happen?

00:33:19.397 --> 00:33:22.867 align:start size:84% position:16%
And the answer was,
"Well, I did the work.

00:33:22.867 --> 00:33:24.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
And in order for
someone to change it,

00:33:24.268 --> 00:33:27.338 align:start size:84% position:16%
they would have
had to rewrite it."

00:33:27.338 --> 00:33:28.773 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then you think,
well, why didn't they?

00:33:28.773 --> 00:33:31.409 align:start size:97% position:3%
And the answer is, well,
they didn't really have time.

00:33:31.409 --> 00:33:33.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
So these things
work in a weird way.

00:33:34.912 --> 00:33:38.483 align:start size:88% position:13%
So this guide to
sustainable development

00:33:38.483 --> 00:33:40.918
has become sort of
a centerpiece of,

00:33:40.918 --> 00:33:42.620
I wouldn't say COP26 exactly,

00:33:42.620 --> 00:33:45.623 align:start size:84% position:16%
but similar
large-scale endeavors

00:33:45.623 --> 00:33:48.259
to sort of steer where
the planet is going.

00:33:48.259 --> 00:33:49.894
Okay, so how was
that put together?

00:33:49.894 --> 00:33:51.596
Well, the UN Secretary General

00:33:51.596 --> 00:33:54.265 align:start size:84% position:16%
nominated a bunch
of ex-presidents and
ex-prime ministers,

00:33:54.265 --> 00:33:56.234
